{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction","text":"Interaction","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag","isActive":true}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"Swami","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"externalID":"Swami","symbolKind":"module","